al decision is to discard J1.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The best move is to discard J1 to focus on forming suited tile melds and pairs, as J1 is a single honor tile with limited utility in the current hand structure.  \nReason: Discarding J1 removes a non-contributing honor tile, preserving the potential for forming multiple chows (e.g., T6-7-8) and pairs (e.g., T1 or B4). The hand\u2019s strength lies in the T and B suits, and retaining these increases the chance of completing a high-point hand.  \nAnswer: Play J1"}
